  "term": "substance dependence",
  "definition": "Substance dependence, also called addiction, is a complex disorder shaped by both environmental and genetic factors. It can involve dependence on substances such as nicotine, alcohol, marijuana, cocaine, opiates, or other drugs, and is linked to serious health and social or economic harm.",
